{
  "id": "25534_shiensuru",
  "headword": "{支援|しえん}する",
  "reading": "しえんする",
  "romaji": "shiensuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to support; to aid; to assist",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to support; to aid; to assist; to back up",
      "explanation": "To provide help, resources, or encouragement to someone or something, typically in a sustained or organized way."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25534_shiensuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{被災者|ひさいしゃ}を{支援|しえん}する。",
      "english": "We support the disaster victims.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25534_shiensuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{政府|せいふ}は{中小企業|ちゅうしょうきぎょう}を{支援|しえん}する{方針|ほうしん}を{発表|はっぴょう}した。",
      "english": "The government announced a policy to support small and medium-sized businesses.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25534_shiensuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "ボランティアが{現地|げんち}に{入|はい}り、{復旧|ふっきゅう}{活動|かつどう}を{支援|しえん}している。",
      "english": "Volunteers have entered the area and are assisting with recovery efforts.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{支援|しえん}する implies organized, sustained help rather than a one-time favor. It is widely used in news, government policy, NGO work, and business contexts. The help may be financial, logistical, emotional, or technical.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {資金|しきん}{支援|しえん}: financial support\n- {技術|ぎじゅつ}{支援|しえん}: technical support\n- {復興|ふっこう}{支援|しえん}: reconstruction aid\n- {子育|こそだ}て{支援|しえん}: childcare support\n- {就職|しゅうしょく}{支援|しえん}: job-hunting assistance\n- {支援|しえん}{団体|だんたい}: support organization\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {援助|えんじょ}する: to aid — often implies material or financial aid, especially in international contexts\n- {応援|おうえん}する: to cheer on; to root for — more personal and emotional, includes cheering at events\n- {助|たす}ける: to help; to rescue — more immediate and personal, often used for direct physical help",
